2. 《中華人民共和國藥典》 (Pharmacopoeia of the People's Republic of China), 2025 edition, Part I
   Reached through TCM-Library (above). Used only as structured facts about herbs (properties, flavours, meridians, functions, cautions). No text of the publication is
   reproduced beyond short factual entries; these records are marked `derived` and have not been reviewed by a practitioner.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Classical Chinese texts — public domain
   The classics quoted in the app are centuries old and in the public domain. Quotations are short and are checked against the source text; the quotation text is shown as it
   appears in the source. Translations and plain-language wording in this product are the project's own.

   Quotations from some books were located in the compilation "TCM-Ancient-Books" (https://github.com/xiaopangxia/TCM-Ancient-Books, git submodule at
   reference/sources/TCM-Ancient-Books). That compilation declares no licence; it is used as a reference for verification only. No file of it is copied, shipped or
   redistributed, and only short quotations of the public-domain texts themselves are used.

